hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1208","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Musa bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, saying: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, and he said Al-Dawrqi: He said: Abu Hayyan told us, Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i told us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Bishr, told us, Abu Hayyan, narrated by Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Bilal at the dawn prayer: “O Bilal! Speak to me.” The most hopeful deed I have ever done will benefit you in Islam, for tonight I heard the sound of your sandals before my hands in Paradise.” He said: “I have not done, O Messenger.” By God, in Islam, I have a deed that I hope will benefit from. I have never purified myself completely at any time of the day or night except that I prayed with that purification. My Lord has not decreed for me to pray"
